OK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","review_id":"T2LKuNTJ85RLZv2DYh0izQ","date":"2018-11-17T00:11:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9527307748794556,"text_excerpt":"We stopped by the French Market for this place. Too bad crawfish wasn't in season to be made boiled :( Nonetheless, the experience was overall good. The boiled shrimps were very tasty, but most people in our party thought it was too spicy. I'm sure you can adjust the spice level (you just have to note it). What I really really liked was the charcoal grilled oysters. I hate raw oysters (don't judge), but these grilled ones were so good! I especially love the cheese on top as well. The only downside was that the wait for the food was a bit long, and we didn't get our drinks until we went back and asked for it. Overall very good!"},{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","review_id":"SBMx9nKYjEl2QQpmwAr2BA","date":"2018-01-22T21:40:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9416284561157227,"text_excerpt":"Ended my trip with J's in the French Market. Coupled with a pint and a pina colada smoothie from the booth to the left, my date and I were ready to take on more oysters. We split an order of jambalaya, a dozen charbroiled oysters, a dozen raw oysters, and a pound of boiled shrimp. The charbroiled oysters were definitely not as good as the ones on Bourbon Street but the raw dozen made up for the others' shortcomings. Skip the shrimp, and come during crawfish season. I got my hopes up thinking crawfish was available off-season as it was still written on the chalkboard menu Definitely made the mistake of not ordering the shrimp and grits--stuff looked mouth watering. This place is expensive ..."},{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","review_id":"Tg34Yc6zxk6YAuyTpUS53A","date":"2018-05-10T12:39:00","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9410448670387268,"text_excerpt":"I tried this place because I was walking through the French Market and wanted some fresh seafood early in the morning. I came at the right time (10 o'clock hour) because they were cooking the crawfish and the aroma it produced was so tempting. My French Market buddy and I ordered two pounds of crawfish and it was the best crawfish I had on my trip (I only ventured through the French quarter). It was hot, juicy, and full of seasoning. If you aren't keen on spicy foods, beware! This is not the crawfish for you. My buddy ordered oysters as well and because we sat at the bar, we were able to watch them shuck them right in front of us. This is great place to go if you want to eat, people watch..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","photo_id":"ztngGTSH3teY46GGRYl3mQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/ztngGTSH3teY46GGRYl3mQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9253895282745361},{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","photo_id":"dws67q1_8ujbeGNabPLI_w","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/dws67q1_8ujbeGNabPLI_w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8408074378967285},{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","photo_id":"BZ1XqphdXHGRVi6e548Ocw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/BZ1XqphdXHGRVi6e548Ocw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8372659087181091},{"business_id":"fsFZQ2ZbTutgUlnWPhTU6A","photo_id":"NmcMVR2VbOEXoEx_vp4hUQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/NmcMVR2